# A card exiled "until [a permanent] leaves the battlefield" returns as a one-shot effect immediately after that permanent
# leaves (CR 610.3), not at the next state-based check - even partway through paying a cost (CR 601.2g-h). Bot1's White
# Auracite has exiled Bot2's Yasharn, Implacable Earth ("Players can't ... sacrifice nonland permanents to cast spells or
# activate abilities"), so Bot1's Ornithopter, equipped with Deconstruction Hammer, may begin "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice
# Deconstruction Hammer" at Bot2's Sol Ring. Bot1 pays the {3} with Krark-Clan Ironworks, sacrificing a Mox Pearl and then
# White Auracite: Yasharn is back on the battlefield the moment the Auracite is gone, so the Hammer can't be sacrificed
# and the activation is taken back (CR 601.2h, 733.1). Everything is as it was before the activation: the Hammer and the
# Auracite still on the battlefield, Yasharn still in exile, the Sol Ring alive and the Ornithopter untapped. The Mox
# Pearl goes first because once Yasharn is back the Ironworks itself could sacrifice nothing more.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
